' Activity Diagram 05 — compute_parents_post_state: derive → scan → backstop.
'
' The merge driver's flow:
'   derive floor(B) → compute Δ → Δ-backstop decision:
'     Δ > 256 : propose PARKS (Err) / validate REJECTS (deterministic, no fork).
'     Δ ≤ 256 : floor-bounded ancestor scan (H3, O(Δ), never cuts above floor)
'               → merge fold (BitmaskOr semilattice + IntegerAdd checked group)
'               → post_state = merge(floor.post_state, band writes).
' The scope-size test |visible_blocks| > 512 is DEMOTED to a metric (not
' node-deterministic) and must never gate admission.
'
' NOTE on node coloring in THIS PlantUML build: the correct form is the suffix
' stereotype  ':label; <<#hex>>'  (verified by rendering).
'
' Source of truth for the H3 fix (section 3.3) in
' docs/casper/theory/finalized-floor/finalized-floor-verification.md.
'
' Render:
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/finalized-floor/diagrams/05-activity-merge-flow.puml

@startuml 05-activity-merge-flow
!theme plain

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor        #FFFFFF
  BorderColor            #333333
  ArrowColor             #444444
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
  DiamondBorderColor     #E65100
}
skinparam legendFontName "monospace"
skinparam legendFontSize 10
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #666666
skinparam defaultFontName "monospace"
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title compute_parents_post_state ── floor derive ▶ floor-bounded scan ▶ Δ-backstop

' Node color legend (suffix <<#hex>> form):
'   blue   (#BBDEFB) = derive / setup step
'   red    (#FFCDD2) = deterministic backstop outcome (park / reject)
'   green  (#C8E6C9 / #A5D6A7) = in-cap scan / fold / final post_state
'   amber diamonds (#FFF8E1)   = decision

start
:derive floor(B)\nover frozen just(B); <<#BBDEFB>>
:Δ = num(maxParent) − num(floor); <<#BBDEFB>>

if (Δ > MAX_FLOOR_DISTANCE (256) ?) then (yes ── backstop)
  note right #FFECB3
    scope-size |visible_blocks| > 512
    is DEMOTED to a metric — NOT
    node-deterministic (branch width
    differs across views), so it must
    NEVER gate admission (only Δ does).
  end note
  if (propose or validate ?) then (propose)
    :PARK the round (Err);\nretry once finality advances\n& Δ shrinks; <<#FFCDD2>>
    kill
  else (validate)
    :block is deterministically INVALID\n(both sides compute the same Δ)\n⟹ REJECT — no fork; <<#FFCDD2>>
    kill
  endif
else (no ── within cap)
  :floor-bounded ancestor scan ──\ncollect band writes with\nblock_number ≥ floor\n(H3, O(Δ), NEVER cuts above floor); <<#C8E6C9>>
  :merge fold ──\nBitmaskOr (semilattice, keep-all-bits)\n+ IntegerAdd (checked group); <<#C8E6C9>>
  :post_state =\nmerge(floor.post_state, band writes); <<#A5D6A7>>
  stop
endif

legend bottom
  Rocq  Selection.scope_covers_band — the floor-bounded scan drops no parent
  write with block_number ≥ floor (H3 coverage), and never cuts above the floor.
  TLA⁺  FinalizedFloorScan.tla — H3 + T-PS over an UNCONSTRAINED parent set;
  MC_FinalizedFloorScan.cfg (BadCut=0) PASSES; _bug.cfg (BadCut=1) is violated.
  The lossy put_cached_parents_post_state substitution was deleted (S5 fix).
endlegend

@enduml
